%% Sequence diagram — Contact form submission via WAHA (self-hosted WhatsApp HTTP API)
%% Pseudo-level: the WAHA call is the only server-side/dynamic flow in the site.
sequenceDiagram
    actor Visitor
    participant Form as ContactForm (client component)
    participant Route as /api/contact (Next.js API route)
    participant Env as Server env (WAHA_API_KEY, WAHA_API_URL, WAHA_SESSION_NAME)
    participant WAHA as Author's self-hosted WAHA instance

    Visitor->>Form: Fill name, phone, message, submit
    Form->>Form: Client-side validation (required fields, phone format)
    Form->>Route: POST { name, phone, message } (HTTPS, no secrets in payload)
    activate Route
    Route->>Route: Validate & sanitize body server-side
    alt validation fails
        Route-->>Form: 400 + error reason
        Form-->>Visitor: Show inline error, keep entered values
    else validation passes
        Route->>Env: Read WAHA_API_KEY / WAHA_API_URL / WAHA_SESSION_NAME
        Route->>WAHA: POST {WAHA_API_URL}/sendText (session=WAHA_SESSION_NAME, key=WAHA_API_KEY, text=composed message)
        activate WAHA
        alt WAHA accepts
            WAHA-->>Route: 2xx (message queued/sent)
            Route-->>Form: 200 success
            Form-->>Visitor: Show "message sent" confirmation
        else WAHA/network error
            WAHA-->>Route: error / timeout
            Route-->>Form: 502 + generic error (no WAHA internals leaked)
            Form-->>Visitor: Show "try again later" + fallback to email/Telegram
        end
        deactivate WAHA
    end
    deactivate Route

    note over Route,Env: WAHA_API_KEY never reaches the browser — read only<br/>inside the API route, which runs server-side only.
